# MEMORY.md — {{ profile.name }}

> _Three-layer: session, positions, signals._

## Layer 1 — Session memory

Per-conversation analytical state. Lives in the agent runtime.

```jsonc
{
  "messages": [...],
  "fetched_in_session": [{"ticker": "...", "ts": "...", "source": "yfinance"}],
  "approvals_granted": [{"action": "...", "ts": "...", "scope": "one-shot"}]
}
```

**Approval scope is `one-shot` by default.** Approval for one trade does not grant approval for the next.

## Layer 2 — Positions (the source of truth on what the user owns)

Schema: `.harness/memory_schemas/positions.json`

```jsonc
{
  "as_of": "2026-05-22T16:00:00-04:00",
  "positions": [
    {"ticker": "AAPL", "shares": 100, "cost_basis_usd": 180.50, "account": "taxable"}
  ]
}
```

**The agent reads this file. The agent does NOT write to it** unless the user has explicitly approved an edit in this session. New positions get added by the user — not by the agent — until the user wires up a synced broker.

## Layer 3 — Signals (the analyst's output)

Schema: `.harness/memory_schemas/signals.json`

```jsonc
{
  "generated_at": "2026-05-22T16:05:00-04:00",
  "signals": [
    {
      "ticker": "AAPL",
      "kind": "overbought",
      "value": 78.6,
      "threshold": 70,
      "indicator": "RSI-14",
      "source": "yfinance",
      "data_as_of": "2026-05-22"
    }
  ]
}
```

This is the agent's **only** mutating output. Signals are write-only-by-agent, read-only-by-user.

## Retention

- Session: discarded on close.
- Positions: kept indefinitely; user-owned.
- Signals: rolling window (default 30 days); older signals archived to `.harness/signals_archive/`.
- **Never persist API keys, account numbers, or PII.**

## Forbidden

- Don't log credentials or trade IDs.
- Don't write to `{{ profile.forbidden_paths | join(", ") }}`.
- Don't infer position quantities — if not in `positions.json`, ask the user.
